  "description": "Follows the Pandavas through forest exile, the instructive stories of Nala and Savitri, the year in disguise and Krishna’s failed peace embassy. Places Arjuna’s crisis and the Bhagavad Gita within the Mahabharata’s conflicts over dharma, divided loyalties, action without attachment, knowledge and devotion, rather than separating the teaching from the decisions that lead to war.",
